.TH DRAGONGL_CLIENT 1 "2026-09-06" "DragonGL 2026.09.04.02" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dragongl_client \- Dragon GL 3D game client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dragongl_client
.I backend
.RI "[ server_ip ]"
.RI "[ port ]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dragongl_client
is the 3D client of the Dragon GL dungeon crawler. It connects to a
.B dragongl_server , lets the player create or load a character, and renders
the dungeon in real time with a graphical in-engine HUD (stats, minimap,
equipment, boss trophies, AR compass).

Unless
.I server_ip
is given on the command line, after selecting the backend the client
interactively prompts for the server IP address (default: 127.0.0.1), the
server password, and the player credentials; new players are then asked to
choose race and class.

The client does not generate a local world at startup: the map is received
from the server in chunks (MSG_MAP_CHUNK), so starting up is fast even
before the first tile is known.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B gl
Start with the OpenGL backend (legacy).
.TP
.B vk
Start with the Vulkan backend (modern), featuring dynamic lighting computed
via SPIR-V shaders.
.TP
.I server_ip
(optional)
IP address or hostname of the game server. When present, the interactive
"Server IP" prompt is skipped (convenient for remote/SSH sessions).
.TP
.I port
(optional)
TCP port of the game server (default 8080).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dragongl_server (1),
.BR dragongl-client (1)
